 ## Background
-The Quadric Error Function (QEF) for sharp features was introduced in the context of dual contouring for isosurface extraction. The method was described in an unofficial source detailing the implementation of an isosurface polygonizer, specifically addressing the limitation of linear systems when dealing with sharp edges where the system is underdetermined [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the general dual contouring framework [Parent](1424-dual-contouring-qef-solver.md).
